### Seeded demo account IDs
# USER       11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111  (starts with 1000.00)
# MERCHANT   22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
# FEES       33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333
# SETTLEMENT 44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444

### Card payment: user pays merchant 100, fee auto-computed (3% => 3.00)
POST http://localhost:8080/transactions/payment
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "payerAccountId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "payeeAccountId": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222",
  "amount": 100.00,
  "idempotencyKey": "pay-0001",
  "description": "POS purchase"
}

### Card payment with explicit fee
POST http://localhost:8080/transactions/payment
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "payerAccountId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "payeeAccountId": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222",
  "amount": 50.00,
  "fee": 1.50,
  "idempotencyKey": "pay-0002"
}

### Refund (partial) of payment pay-0001 -> use the returned transaction id
POST http://localhost:8080/transactions/refund
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "originalTransactionId": "REPLACE_WITH_PAYMENT_TX_ID",
  "amount": 40.00,
  "idempotencyKey": "refund-0001"
}

### Wallet transfer
POST http://localhost:8080/transactions/transfer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccountId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "toAccountId": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222",
  "amount": 25.00,
  "idempotencyKey": "transfer-0001"
}

### Merchant settlement (full balance when amount omitted)
POST http://localhost:8080/transactions/settlement
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "merchantAccountId": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222",
  "settlementAccountId": "44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444",
  "idempotencyKey": "settle-0001"
}

### Account ledger statement
GET http://localhost:8080/accounts/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111/ledger

### Account balance
GET http://localhost:8080/accounts/22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

### Reconciliation
GET http://localhost:8080/reconciliation

### Create a new account (e.g. EUR for multi-currency testing)
POST http://localhost:8080/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "EU Merchant",
  "type": "MERCHANT",
  "currency": "EUR"
}
